    "node_id": "C_kwDOQ2BT6NoAKDNhY2Q2YjQ1Yjc1NmFmM2NhN2Y4Y2M5MWI4ZGNjYThjNTZhZTg0NGM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Radim Krčmář",
        "email": "rkrcmar@qti.qualcomm.com",
        "date": "2026-02-05T15:31:11Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Radim Krčmář",
        "email": "rkrcmar@qti.qualcomm.com",
        "date": "2026-02-05T15:52:37Z"
      },
      "message": "ISA-architecture: align acecrstatus with sstatus.ACES\n\nWe want a higher granularity tracking of CR state, but we can keep the\nexisting status.ACES design, just make it work per-CR.  To align with\nthe s/vs status.ACES design, there are two CSRs, s/vs acecrstatus.\n\nWe can add m acecrstatus if we want to optimize supervisor domain\ncontext switches as well, but I don't think it makes sense to remove vs,\nbecause there isn't much diffrence between U-mode and VS-mode context\nswitches in frequency nor implementation.\n\nI have omitted the hardware change to Initial, since it's currently\nmissing from status.ACES as well.\nCurrently, hardware only changes to Dirty, so software can decide what\nboth Initial and Clean denote.\n\nDue to presence of ace.reset and ace.clean, I think it makes sense to\nspecify Initial to be the state that ace.reset and ace.clean provide.",
